<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        Printed-check positioning and content tweaks requested by UFS.

        Injected as a small stylesheet into the check face template
        (l10n_us_check_printing.ckus_check). A style tag rendered anywhere on
        the page applies to the whole printout, so this one block reaches the
        check face, the stubs, and the page wrapper.

        IMPORTANT, learned the hard way: the check report is a qweb-pdf report,
        rendered by wkhtmltopdf. Its old WebKit engine SILENTLY DROPS CSS
        transforms (translate/translateY), so an earlier version that nudged
        the fields with `transform: translateY(...)` moved them in the browser
        preview but NOT in the printed PDF. wkhtmltopdf does honor absolute
        `top` and box `margin`, which is how the whole layout positions itself
        (every field is `position: absolute; top: <n>in`). So all positioning
        here uses margin/top, never transform.

        1. Move the whole printout down one spacing (0.25 in). The page article
           is positioned by the company Check Margins as `position: relative;
           top: 0.125in`. We add a 0.25 in top margin on top of that, so the
           check and both stubs shift down together and the company setting
           still works as a further nudge. UFS reported every field printing a
           quarter inch too high on their pre-printed stock.

        2. Move the payee address down two more spacings (0.5 in) so it lands
           in the #9 window. The layout puts it at top: 1.65in; we override to
           2.15in. This is on top of the page-wide 0.25 in, so the address ends
           up three quarters of an inch lower than the base layout and half an
           inch below the rest of the check face.

        3. Remove the invoices from the check face. When a check pays several
           bills their numbers render on the memo line of the check itself
           (.ckus_memo). display:none is honored by wkhtmltopdf, so this always
           worked; the remittance stub keeps the itemized list.

        Covers the pre-printed Print Check (Top) layout UFS uses. The margins
        are calibrated to their check stock; the two values (0.25in page margin
        and the 2.15in address top) are the knobs to nudge on the next test
        print. Blank Check and Middle/Bottom layouts would need their own
        overrides.
    -->
    <template id="ckus_check_ufs_tweaks"
              inherit_id="l10n_us_check_printing.ckus_check">
        <xpath expr="//div[hasclass('ckus_check')]" position="inside">
            <style>
                .ckus_top_page { margin-top: 0.25in !important; }
                .ckus_check { transform: none !important; }
                .ckus_payee_addr { top: 2.15in !important; transform: none !important; }
                .ckus_memo { display: none !important; }
            </style>
        </xpath>
    </template>
</odoo>
